WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.990
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.816
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.116 --> 00:00:15.414
Unit nineteen: Renewable Energy. Today you will compare energy sources with comparatives.

4
00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.529
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.827
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:25.253
Renewable energy.

7
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.770
Renewable energy means energy from sources that never run out.

8
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.441
Renewable energy is the future.

9
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.364
Your turn. Say: Renewable energy.

10
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.118
Renewable energy.

11
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:43.140
Solar power.

12
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.637
Solar power means energy from the sun.

13
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.342
Our school uses solar power.

14
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.997
Your turn. Say: Solar power.

15
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:56.985
Solar power.

16
00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:58.914
Wind turbine.

17
00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:03.495
Wind turbine means a tall machine that makes electricity from wind.

18
00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:06.501
Wind turbines spin on the hills.

19
00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:09.537
Your turn. Say: Wind turbine.

20
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.900
Wind turbine.

21
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:15.721
Fossil fuel.

22
00:01:16.717 --> 00:01:20.423
Fossil fuel means coal, oil or gas from under the ground.

23
00:01:21.017 --> 00:01:23.074
Fossil fuels pollute the air.

24
00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.649
Your turn. Say: Fossil fuel.

25
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:30.849
Fossil fuel.

26
00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:32.689
Sustainable.

27
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:37.227
Sustainable means able to continue without harming the planet.

28
00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:40.443
Bamboo is a sustainable material.

29
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:44.016
Your turn. Say: Sustainable.

30
00:01:46.867 --> 00:01:48.065
Sustainable.

31
00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:49.678
Emission.

32
00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:52.985
Emission means gas sent into the air.

33
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:55.606
Cars produce harmful emissions.

34
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:58.823
Your turn. Say: Emission.

35
00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:02.598
Emission.

36
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.525
Clean energy.

37
00:02:05.517 --> 00:02:08.491
Clean energy means energy that does not pollute.

38
00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:10.944
Clean energy protects our health.

39
00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:14.864
Your turn. Say: Clean energy.

40
00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.701
Clean energy.

41
00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:20.474
Resource.

42
00:02:21.483 --> 00:02:24.365
Resource means something useful that people use.

43
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.926
Water is a precious resource.

44
00:02:27.517 --> 00:02:30.726
Your turn. Say: Resource.

45
00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:34.777
Resource.

46
00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:39.229
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:43.430
Visal, why is renewable energy important for the future?

48
00:02:44.517 --> 00:02:48.478
Because solar power is cleaner than fossil fuels.

49
00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:50.863
Is it cheaper too?

50
00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:57.235
Yes, it's cheaper than before, and Cambodia has lots of sun!

51
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.013
What about wind turbines?

52
00:03:01.117 --> 00:03:06.181
They're quieter than I thought, and they produce fewer emissions than coal.

53
00:03:07.333 --> 00:03:09.054
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.917 --> 00:03:12.195
Grammar focus: Comparatives.

55
00:03:12.495 --> 00:03:13.717
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.417 --> 00:03:17.182
Solar power is cleaner than fossil fuels.

57
00:03:18.083 --> 00:03:20.675
Wind power is more sustainable than coal.

58
00:03:21.583 --> 00:03:23.896
Clean energy is better for our health than oil.

59
00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:29.181
Use -er for short adjectives and 'more' for long ones. Always use 'than'.

60
00:03:29.917 --> 00:03:34.868
Be careful! Don't say: Solar power is cleaner then fossil fuels.

61
00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:40.516
Say: Solar power is cleaner than fossil fuels.

62
00:03:40.816 --> 00:03:43.292
Use 'than', not 'then', in comparisons.

63
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.671
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:49.002
Power for the Future.

65
00:03:49.302 --> 00:03:52.892
Renewable energy includes solar power and wind turbines.

66
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.979
It is a sustainable alternative to fossil fuels.

67
00:03:57.967 --> 00:04:00.663
Solar power is cleaner than coal and oil.

68
00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:05.048
Clean energy resources help reduce harmful emissions.

69
00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:08.706
Renewable energy protects our planet's future.

70
00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.720
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:14.583 --> 00:04:17.547
Solar power is cleaner blank fossil fuels.

72
00:04:17.847 --> 00:04:20.676
A, than. B, then. C, that.

73
00:04:24.233 --> 00:04:26.059
The answer is A: than.

74
00:04:27.217 --> 00:04:29.251
Coal, oil and gas are blank.

75
00:04:29.551 --> 00:04:34.424
A, fossil fuels. B, renewable energy. C, clean energy.

76
00:04:37.967 --> 00:04:40.686
The answer is A: fossil fuels.

77
00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.850
Gas sent into the air is an blank.

78
00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:47.745
A, emission. B, resource. C, turbine.

79
00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.346
The answer is A: emission.

80
00:04:54.533 --> 00:04:57.662
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:58.517 --> 00:05:01.329
Why is renewable energy important for the future?

82
00:05:10.117 --> 00:05:11.605
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:11.905 --> 00:05:21.257
Renewable energy is important because it is cleaner and safer than fossil fuels. It will keep the air healthier for the next generation.

84
00:05:21.557 --> 00:05:23.266
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:27.929
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and comparatives.

86
00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:34.666
Today's value is environmental responsibility. Small green actions at home help the whole planet.

87
00:05:34.966 --> 00:05:37.479
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

88
00:05:37.779 --> 00:05:40.419
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

